    <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="f-823" contextRef="c-02">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;1 - 2. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Respondent is engaged in the operation of an interstate natural gas transmission line. Fayetteville Express Pipeline LLC consists of approximately 185 miles of a single 42-inch diameter pipeline extending from Conway County, Arkansas to the Russell Compressor Station with the capacity of 2.0 billion cubic feet per day (&amp;quot;Bcf/day&amp;quot;) with a maximum allowable operating pressure (&amp;quot;MAOP&amp;quot;) of 1,160 psi; and a single 42-inch diameter pipeline with capacity of 2.0 Bcf/day and an MAOP of 1,480 psi from the discharge of the Russell Compressor Station to the terminus of the pipeline in Panola County, Mississippi. The Russell Compressor Station consists of 10 compressor units with a combined 71,464 horsepower. There are 15 receipt measurement stations and 4 delivery measurement stations with no current active flow on the system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;3. No scheduled flows on this transmission line.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
