        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-119_46956_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold"></b></span></span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold"></b></span></span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold"><em><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">Schedule Page: 278   Line No.: 1   Column: a</span></em></b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">In December 2017, the "Tax Cuts and Jobs Act" was signed into law. Among other provisions, the highest corporate federal income tax rate was reduced from 35% to 21% for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2017. Under regulatory accounting, the effect on deferred tax assets and liabilities of a change in tax rate is recognized as a regulatory asset or regulatory liability in the period that includes the enactment date.</span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"><span> <span> </span></span></span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">Docket No. PL19-21-000 dated November 15, 2018</span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">.</span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"><span> </span></span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">The amortization period is 26 years.</span></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-121_46957_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold"><em>Schedule Page: 278   Line No.: 2   Column: a</em></b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Pursuant to Section 36 of the General Terms and Conditions of Fayetteville Express Pipeline's FERC Gas Tariff, First Revised Volume No. 1, Docket No. RP25-112-000, as approved by FERC's order issued on November 19, 2024, <span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">Docket No. </span>RP25-856-000, <span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">as approved by FERC's order issued on<span> May 21, 2025, and Docket No. RP26-120-000, <span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">as approved by FERC's order issued on<span> November 18, 2025.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-201_46958_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 7.5pt; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1)">Schedule Page: 234 Line No.: 5 Column: b</span></b></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1)"><br /></span></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0 0 7.5pt; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span><span><span><span><span><span>Estimated balances of deferred income taxes that could be included in the development of jurisdictional recourse rates at 1/1/2025: None</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-202_46960_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Schedule Page: 274 Line No: 5 Column: b</b></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Estimated balances of deferred income taxes that could be included in the development of jurisdictional recourse rates at 1/1/2025:</span></span></p><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="368" class="e-rte-table-border e-rte-table" style="width: 276pt"> <tr style="height: 15pt"><td height="20" width="245" style="height: 15pt; width: 184pt; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif">Tax/Book  Depreciation</td><td width="23" style="width: 17pt; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif">$</td><td width="100" style="width: 75pt; padding: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-align: right"><span> </span>93,849,144 </td></tr><tr style="height: 15pt"><td height="20" style="height: 15pt; padding: 0; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif">Tax/Book Gain on Sale of  Assets</td><td style="padding: 0; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-s